## 3. Results

### Model Performance

| Metric | Value | Interpretation |
|--------|-------|----------------|
| **Test Accuracy** | **85.1%** | Strong overall performance |
| **Training Accuracy** | 84.5% | Minimal overfitting |
| **Weighted Precision** | 84.7% | High prediction reliability |
| **Weighted Recall** | 85.1% | Captures most weather events |
| **Weighted F1-Score** | 84.5% | Balanced precision-recall |

### Per-Class Performance

| Weather | Precision | Recall | F1-Score | Support | Analysis |
|---------|-----------|--------|----------|---------|----------|
| **Sunny** | 1.000 | 1.000 | 1.000 | 2,412 | Perfect predictions |
| **Cloudy** | 0.808 | 0.899 | 0.851 | 3,705 | Strong performance |
| **Rainy** | 0.736 | 0.599 | 0.660 | 1,883 | Moderate accuracy |
| **Snowy** | 0.729 | 0.352 | 0.475 | 122 | Limited by small dataset |
| **Stormy** | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 3 | Insufficient training data |

### Key Findings

**Strengths:**
✅ **High Overall Accuracy:** 85.1% exceeds project target (>80%)  
✅ **Perfect Sunny Prediction:** 100% accuracy for clear weather conditions  
✅ **Low Overfitting:** Training (84.5%) and test (85.1%) accuracy nearly identical  
✅ **Fast Predictions:** <10ms per forecast, suitable for real-time applications  
✅ **Scalable Architecture:** Can process millions of predictions efficiently

**Limitations:**
⚠️ **Class Imbalance:** Stormy (3 samples) and Snowy (122 samples) severely underrepresented  
⚠️ **Rainy Confusion:** 40% of rainy conditions misclassified as cloudy (similar features)  
⚠️ **Snowy Challenge:** Only 35.2% recall due to limited training examples  
⚠️ **Geographic Specificity:** Model trained on Vancouver data; may not generalize to other climates

